    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-29",
      "edition": "Sunday 29 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Playmaker wing",
          "heading": "Wainiqolo sets up all three Fiji tries in 23-21 loss to Italy",
          "body": "The right wing drove Fiji's attack in Friday's 11th-place final at Twickenham. His long cut-out pass sent Ponipate Loganimasi weaving through for the first try. After the break he put fellow wing Peniasi Dakuwaqa over, then released No. 8 Kitione Salawa in the 55th minute as Fiji overturned a 17-0 deficit to lead 21-20. Caleb Muntz converted all three, but a scrum penalty on the edge of Fiji's 22 let Tommaso Allan kick the winner with 13 minutes left."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England start Fin Smith at fly-half in All Blacks play-off",
          "body": "Springboks' Rassie Erasmus serving six-match World Rugby ban. Scarlets appoint former Wales centre Scott Williams as academy skills coach. Argentina lose Mayco Vivas to red card in France loss."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-29",
      "edition": "Sunday 29 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Bench call",
          "heading": "Borthwick names Marcus Smith and Henry Pollock among All Blacks play-off replacements",
          "body": "Steve Borthwick's bench for Saturday's Nations Championship third-place play-off against New Zealand at Twickenham ran Jamie George, Fin Baxter, Will Stuart, George Martin, Ben Curry, Pollock, Archie McParland and the Harlequins playmaker, with Fin Smith starting at fly-half and Maro Itoje captaining the side. England reached the play-off after winning five of their six pool matches to finish second in the northern hemisphere table, a point behind France, and came in off the previous weekend's 37-12 win over the All Blacks."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks' Rassie Erasmus serving six-match World Rugby ban",
          "body": "Scarlets appoint former Wales centre Scott Williams as academy skills coach. Argentina lose Mayco Vivas to red card in France loss."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "WalesOnline"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-29",
      "edition": "Sunday 29 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Defensive overhaul",
          "heading": "Geoffrey Doumayrou overhauls France's defence with outside-in rush and lineout roles",
          "body": "Rugbyrama credits France's new defence coach with the solidity that carried Les Bleus through an injury-hit autumn. His rush defence uses very low body positions that flirt with the limits of the law. Since November the outermost defenders have switched to outside-in framing to hit ball carriers. Every forward now knows his post when defending four-, five-, six- or seven-man lineouts, long a structural weakness. Mickaël Guillard said the squad now knows how many players fold after the first ruck."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England start Fin Smith at fly-half in All Blacks play-off",
          "body": "Springboks' Rassie Erasmus serving six-match World Rugby ban. Scarlets appoint former Wales centre Scott Williams as academy skills coach. Argentina lose Mayco Vivas to red card in France loss."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Allianz Stadium, Twickenham"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-29",
      "edition": "Sunday 29 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fly-half form",
          "heading": "Sam Prendergast's perfect kicking and cross-kick steer Ireland past Wallabies 38-14",
          "body": "The fly-half was flawless off the tee in Friday's win at Allianz Stadium, Twickenham — five conversions and a penalty for 13 points — and his crossfield kick put Rob Baloucoune over for Ireland's third try. Planet Rugby rated Prendergast hugely impressive across November, saying he ran the show and calmly took the right options, while Ireland finished the month with four wins from four. Of the 45 fans in the app who answered after full time, 91% were buzzing."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England start Fin Smith at fly-half in All Blacks play-off",
          "body": "Springboks' Rassie Erasmus serving six-match World Rugby ban. Scarlets appoint former Wales centre Scott Williams as academy skills coach. Argentina lose Mayco Vivas to red card in France loss."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-29",
      "edition": "Sunday 29 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coach's call",
          "heading": "Gonzalo Quesada concedes Italy had other options than kicking deep against Fiji",
          "body": "Asked about kicking long in the closing stages of Friday's 23-21 win over Fiji at Twickenham, Quesada accepted that, on review, different solutions can be found. At the time, he explained, Italy believed they could win a penalty from the drive. The aim was to keep play out of their own half, trusting the defence and the players on the field to regain possession. Fiji, ahead 21-20 until Tommaso Allan's penalty with 13 minutes left, were held out to the final whistle."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
